 # Code Review
@@ -64,9 +65,44 @@ user commit unaware that open findings exist.
 - `--fix`: after reporting, apply fixes for the confirmed findings directly to the working
   tree, then re-run the affected checks (typecheck/tests) to confirm the fix didn't break
   anything. Do not silently fix — tell the user what was changed and why.
+- `--commit`: after the review (and the fixes, if `--fix` was also passed), commit the reviewed
+  diff locally — see Step 5. It applies **only** when `--commit` is literally in this
+  invocation's arguments; never infer it from the conversation ("revisar antes de commitar" is
+  a request to review, not `--commit`).
+
+## Step 5 — Commit (only with `--commit`)
+
+Runs last, after Step 3 and `--fix`. Check the gates in order. At the first one that fails,
+**do not commit**: tell the user which gate failed and why, then stop — they decide what's next.
+
+1. **There is something to commit.** If the diff is empty or trivial (see Rules), say there was
+   nothing to commit.
+2. **No open findings.** Every confirmed finding was fixed. If any remains open — including
+   because `--fix` wasn't passed — list them and say no commit was made.
+3. **The project's pre-commit checks pass** after the fixes. Take them from the reviewed
+   project's AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md (e.g. typecheck, tests, build) and run all of them. If none
+   are documented, run the evident ones (e.g. the `typecheck`/`test` scripts in package.json)
+   and name them in the reply. Any failure — a failing pre-commit hook included — means no
+   commit: report the failing command and the relevant part of its output.
+
+When every gate passes:
+
+- **What goes in**: the whole reviewed diff (the original work plus your fixes), not only the
+  fixes. Stage by explicit path — `git add -- <paths>` with just the files in the review scope —
+  and commit those same paths (`git commit -m "<message>" -- <paths>`), so nothing else that
+  happened to be staged rides along. Never `git add -A` / `git add .` (other agents may be
+  editing the same tree), and never stage `.env` files, credentials or secrets.
+- **Message**: Conventional Commits (`type(scope): summary`), in the language of the repo's
+  history (check `git log --oneline -10`), following any commit rules in the project's
+  AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md. No `Co-Authored-By` trailer unless the project's `.claude/settings.json`
+  sets `attribution.commit`.
+- **Where**: the current branch. No new branch, no push, no `--amend`, no `--no-verify`.
+- Finish by showing what was committed: `git log -1 --stat`.
 
 ## Rules
 
 - Never invent findings to pad the list — an empty result is a valid, good outcome.
 - Don't flag style/formatting preferences already enforced by lint/prettier.
 - If the diff is empty or trivial (e.g. a one-line typo fix), say so and skip the full pass.
+- Without `--commit`, never stage or commit anything — not even after `--fix`. The commit is the
+  user's call.
